module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.entry_scoped_typecheck_rss_tracks_the_name_census

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data entry_scoped_typecheck_rss_tracks_the_name_census: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "entry_scoped_typecheck_rss_tracks_the_name_census" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an `--entry` typecheck's resident set tracks the name census of every `--source-root`, not the reference-derived closure the CLI reports as the subject** (INVALID STATE: `gunbc compile --entry` prints `resolved N sources (reference-derived closure …), M indexed modules in the name census only` with N much smaller than M, and typecheck still builds `v1_compiler.cli_run` `tree_bare_census_for_root` over the containing root's whole-tree compile closure plus the process-shared index of M modules. The stall diagnostic then names one small module as if that module's import graph were the demand. HARM: a reader sizes a runner, a budget raise, or a hub-import split against N, while RSS is O(M). On srv4 that mis-sizing is MemoryStallRefusedPageThrash at the admitted 16 GiB line.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT, MEASURED 2026-09-11 by session sleek-swift-789 on this tree, locally (BuildBuddy cannot read the host budget). Binary: arm64 `gunbc` from 2026-09-11 04:12 (this session had no release binary). Peak from `/proc/<pid>/status` VmHWM because `/usr/bin/time` is absent. Invocation matching the floor's roots and the stall text's `--entry` remedy: `gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/workflow/floor2_prepared_subject.dag --target dag`. Completing run, exit 0. Peak RSS 9964140 KiB = 9.73 GiB. Wall 184 s, of which compile.reconcile 60 s. Compiler line: `resolved 16 sources (reference-derived closure entry=src/v2/workflow/floor2_prepared_subject.dag), 5385 indexed modules in the name census only`. The 16 sources match the authored import closure of `v2.workflow.floor2_prepared_subject` (v2.std.algebra, collection, logic, node and their std imports — it does not import `v2.workflow.required_floor`). Declaration-like rows in those 16 files ~730; under the same two roots ~5401 `.dag` files.",

    "THE FLOOR SPECIMEN THIS MEASUREMENT PRICES, so the isolated number is not mistaken for the floor's working set. Required-witnesses-floor runs 34559858878 and 34563510604 (two srv4 hosts) refused MemoryStallRefusedPageThrash while typechecking `v2.workflow.floor2_prepared_subject` (305405 and 301817 major faults/min, 4% of wall, ~31 s window, admitted 16106127360 bytes from cgroup memory.high, swap off, typed-cache evictions in window 0). The refusal entry is `src/v2/workflow/floor_terminal_ledger_wire.dag`, which imports both this module and `v2.workflow.required_floor`. So the named module's typecheck runs late inside a process that already indexed the parse universe (5439 files on that run) and holds a large typed cache. Isolated 9.73 GiB plus that resident state exceeds 16 GiB. Near-identical across hosts because N, M, and the census are deterministic.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a stall or budget argument names one `--entry` module, join the CLI's N (closure) to its M (census) before asking whether that module imported a hub. If N is small and M is the corpus, the demand is the census construction (`tree_bare_census_for_root`, process-shared index), not the import graph. The 2026-08-28 scoped control cited on `gunbc.whole_corpus_compile_admission` (src/v2/std/node.dag at 5.5 GiB) is the same grain: node is inside this 16-file closure; a larger N of 16 still paid M=5385 and 9.73 GiB.",

    "BOUNDED AGAINST THREE NEIGHBOURS. It is NOT `absent_reads_identically_to_never_looked`: that class is that census-only modules are never judged; this class is that they are still paid in RSS. It is NOT a hub re-export of `required_floor` by floor2_prepared_subject — that import is absent; the wire that failed is the hub, and splitting it would not drop an isolated `--entry` of floor2 below the census cost. It is NOT the 2026-08-17 per-claim CPU shrink-only ruling: memory admission is a different subject, and a raise still needs measured srv4 headroom beside this peak. Isolated 9.73 GiB already consumes most of the 16 GiB class; there is no srv4 RSS sample before this typecheck on which to claim headroom. Raising is therefore the pattern that ruling names, with the cost-shape unfixed.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The stall refuses typed and located. The invalid cost-shape remains writable.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: mechanically preventable. Whether typecheck RSS is charged to the closure or to the census is a fact of `compile_emission` / `tree_bare_census_for_root`; a check can refuse an `--entry` whose M/N ratio and peak disagree with the closure grain, or the construction can stop forcing the whole-root census on an Entry subject. It is not structurally impossible: indexing the pool for bare-name parity is a legitimate construction; the defect is charging its resident set to a 16-module typecheck as if it were that module's work.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: typecheck of an Entry subject holds a symbol index whose bare census is the reference-derived closure (or a shared process-wide census that is not cloned into the Entry typecheck), sufficient that a 16-source `--entry` of floor2_prepared_subject with the same two roots peaks far below the 16 GiB srv4 line on a cold process. Until then this class is found by measuring, which is why the 9.73 GiB reading is filed here rather than used to raise the floor budget. Floor budget rows and parse witnesses are a different lane.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
